From: arch-port
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: nxp-nci: don't unregister under info_lock

nxp_nci_remove() held info_lock across nci_unregister_device(). When the
device is still up (neard keeps it powered), unregistering closes it
through nxp_nci_close(), which takes info_lock again: the unbind (or
module removal) hangs in D state in nxp_nci_close and the device lock
stays held, so a later reboot blocks in device_shutdown.

Unregister first, then put the chip in cold mode under the lock, and
free the nci device last.

diff --git a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
index 448e5a4e7..08c09dc84 100644
--- a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
@@ -186,15 +186,20 @@ void nxp_nci_remove(struct nci_dev *ndev)
 		nxp_nci_fw_work_complete(info, -ESHUTDOWN);
 	cancel_work_sync(&info->fw_info.work);
 
+	/*
+	 * Not under info_lock: unregistering closes a device that is still
+	 * up, and nxp_nci_close() takes the lock itself.
+	 */
+	nci_unregister_device(ndev);
+
 	mutex_lock(&info->info_lock);
 
 	if (info->phy_ops->set_mode)
 		info->phy_ops->set_mode(info->phy_id, NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD);
 
-	nci_unregister_device(ndev);
-	nci_free_device(ndev);
-
 	mutex_unlock(&info->info_lock);
+
+	nci_free_device(ndev);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(nxp_nci_remove);
 
